src/polymarket_weather/__pycache__/
src/polymarket_weather/polymarket/
# Data policy: live-collected, NON-reproducible series are committed (market snapshots,
# price history, forecast/ensemble/multi-model snapshots — the track record depends on
# them; a missed snapshot can never be refetched). Archives that CAN be refetched from
# their sources at any time stay untracked:
#   *_historical_*.csv  — previous-runs leads / station truth / ERA5 features
#   *_obs_hourly.csv    — hourly METARs (IEM)
#   *_nbm.csv           — NBM guidance (IEM archive)
src/polymarket_weather/data/weather/*_historical_*.csv
src/polymarket_weather/data/weather/*_obs_hourly.csv
src/polymarket_weather/data/weather/*_nbm.csv
# EXCEPTION — the daily settlement-truth actuals ARE committed as a resilience fallback.
# They are small (~200KB/city, daily) and the grading of the ENTIRE dashboard depends on
# them; the IEM feed 503s intermittently and a fresh cloud runner has no other copy, so a
# transient outage was dropping whole cities. Committed here, fetch_historical_truth "keeps
# the existing CSV" on a failed refetch and the build stays complete. truth-eval refreshes
# and re-commits them daily, so the fallback never goes more than ~1 day stale.
!src/polymarket_weather/data/weather/*_historical_actuals.csv
output/logs/

